    (0, None, '\'Viktor Petrovich, I completely forgot.\' "Zabyla", "forgot", ends in -la because Vika is a woman. "Sovsem" is "completely". She uses his name and father\'s name, polite and formal.'),
    (1, None, '\'Here is the cash for fresh caviar.\' "Ikra", caviar, is a feminine word, so "fresh" is "svezhuyu", ending in -uyu after "na". "Nalichnye" is the cash word from the bet scene.'),
    (2, None, '\'Thank you very much, my dear Vika.\' "Ogromnoe spasibo", "huge thank-you", is how Russians say "thanks a lot". "Dorogaya" is "dear", and also "expensive". Barinov pours on the charm.'),
    (3, None, '\'You are saving our evening banquet.\' "Spasaesh", "you save", is from the family of "spasibo", which started as "God save". "Vecherny" is "evening" as a describing word, from "vecher".'),
    (4, None, '\'The supplier will bring the jar in an hour.\' "Postavshchik", "supplier", is from "postavlyat", "to supply", a relative of "postavit", "put". "Cherez chas" is "in an hour". "Banka" is a jar.'),
    (5, None, '\'Excellent, I will meet the courier myself.\' "Vstrechu" is "I will meet", for someone who arrives. "Kurera" is "kurer", courier, with -a, because he\'s the one being met. Barinov\'s offer is a little too eager.'),
    (6, None, '\'Please give him the money right away.\' "Otdayte" is "give over", the polite "hand it over", and "emu" is "to him". "Srazu" is "right away". Vika is careful, as she always is.'),
    (7, None, '\'Do not worry, everything is under my control.\' "Ne perezhivay", "don\'t worry", is from "perezhivat", "live through", the word for stress. "Pod moim kontrolem" is "under my control", and both words take endings after "pod".'),
    (8, None, '\'And what is going on with our stove?\' "Tam", "there", in the middle is a filler. "S nashey plitoy" is "with our stove": "plita" becomes "plitoy" after "s". Vika asks again, because she doesn\'t believe the first answer.'),
    (9, None, '\'The craftsmen are already finishing the complex repair.\' "Zakanchivayut" is "are finishing", the ongoing form of "zakonchit". "Slozhny" is "complex" and also "difficult". "Remont" is any repair.'),
    (10, None, '\'I rely on your honesty, chef.\' "Nadeyus na", "hope on", is the Russian for "rely on". "Chestnost", "honesty", grows from "chestny", "honest". It\'s a trust he does not deserve.'),
